    "readThisFirst": "`live` is what the page runs. `source.authoredConfig` is what the plugin ships. `probe` is that config read back off a real pJS instance instantiated in the page this run. authoredConfig and probe disagree on purpose: particles.js with `retina_detect: true` multiplies size.value, line_linked.distance, line_linked.width, move.speed and every interactivity mode distance by window.devicePixelRatio at init. The probe ran at dpr 2, so those five families of number are exactly doubled. Copy authoredConfig into a reimplementation; expect probe's values at 2x.",
    "WARNING": "particles.js is enqueued sitewide and never initialises. live.instanceCount is 0; the page has zero canvas elements. The probe block and the SYNTHETIC-* frames were produced by force-instantiating the plugin bundled preset and describe an effect that does not exist on this site. The real animated background is the <video> in the video block."
